window.CALTPA.rubricLevels={"ms-math": [["Candidate does not use information from recent math learning* to plan instruction. Candidate does not select an age-/grade-level appropriate CA State Math Content Strand/Standard and/or a Math Practice Standard or they select a strand/standard that is more than one grade level above or below the students they plan to teach. Candidate does not develop a math learning goal** that is based on the selected math strand/standard and/or does not include math content and/or practice. Candidate does not develop a math ALD learning goal or the ALD learning goal does not align with the math learning goal. Candidate does not describe how they will create a safe, positive learning environment or does not describe how the environment will support students during the math lesson. Candidate does not describe how they will leverage the students\u2019 assets and/or interests. Candidate does not describe how they will engage students in higher-order thinking*** to deepen their math understanding. Candidate does not describe how they will monitor student learning during the math lesson. Candidate does not describe how they will use UDL-focused instructional strategy(ies) to support student learning.", "Candidate vaguely uses information from recent math learning* to plan instruction. Candidate selects an age-/grade- level appropriate CA State Math Content Strand/Standard and/or a Math Practice Standard that is either one grade-level above or below the students they plan to teach. Candidate develops a math learning goal** that is vaguely based on the selected math strand/standard and includes math content and practice. Candidate develops a math ALD learning goal that vaguely aligns with the math learning goal. Candidate vaguely describes how they will create a safe, positive learning environment or vaguely describes how the learning environment will support students during the math lesson. Candidate vaguely describes how they will leverage the students\u2019 assets and/or interests. Candidate vaguely describes how they will engage students in higher-order thinking*** to deepen their math understanding. Candidate vaguely describes how they will monitor student learning during the math lesson. Candidate vaguely describes how they will use UDL-focused instructional strategy(ies) to support student learning.", "Candidate clearly uses information from recent math learning* to plan instruction. Candidate selects an age-/grade- level appropriate CA State Math Content Strand/Standard and a Math Practice Standard for the students they plan to teach. Candidate develops a math learning goal** that is clearly based on the selected math strand/standard and includes both math content and practice. Candidate develops a math ALD learning goal that clearly aligns with the math learning goal. Candidate describes how they will create a safe, positive learning environment that clearly supports students during the math lesson. Candidate clearly describes how they will leverage the students\u2019 assets and/or interests. Candidate clearly describes how they will engage students in higher-order thinking*** to deepen their math understanding. Candidate clearly describes how they will monitor student learning during the math lesson. Candidate clearly describes how they will use UDL-focused instructional strategy(ies) to support student learning.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s planning clearly includes opportunities for students to learn collaboratively to progress toward the math content and practice and math ALD learning goals.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate designs a math lesson that reflects the interconnectedness of math plus an additional academic content area (e.g., literacy, social science, art, science, PE)."], ["Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS1 are not based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) do not leverage FS1\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) do not support FS1\u2019s math ALD learning need(s) through reading, writing, listening, and/or speaking.", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS1 are vaguely based on recent learning* or information used is not recent. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) vaguely leverage FS1\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) vaguely support FS1\u2019s math ALD learning need(s) through reading, writing, listening, and/or speaking.", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS1 are clearly based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) clearly leverage FS1\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) clearly support FS1\u2019s math ALD learning need(s) through reading, writing, listening, and/or speaking.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate plans adaptation(s) for FS1 to participate in the math lesson by using multiple modes of communication** to support FS1\u2019s learning needs.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate\u2019s planning for FS1\u2019s adaptation(s) draws upon and/or refers to evidence- based practice(s) and/or research appropriate to FS1\u2019s math ALD."], ["Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS2 are not based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) do not leverage FS2\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) do not support FS2\u2019s math learning need(s).**", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS2 are vaguely based on recent learning* or information used is not recent. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) vaguely leverage FS2\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) vaguely support FS2\u2019s math learning need(s).**", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS2 are clearly based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) clearly leverage FS2\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) clearly support FS2\u2019s math learning need(s).**", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate plans adaptation(s) for FS2 to participate in the math lesson by using two or more multisensory strategies*** to support FS2\u2019s learning needs.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate\u2019s planning for FS2\u2019s adaptation(s) draws upon and/or refers to evidence- based math practice(s) and/or research appropriate to FS2\u2019s math learning need(s)."], ["Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS3 are not based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) do not leverage FS3\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) do not support FS3\u2019s well-being and/or behavior to meet their math learning need(s).", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS3 are vaguely based on recent learning* or information used is not recent. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) vaguely leverage FS3\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) vaguely support FS3\u2019s well-being and/or behavior to meet their math learning need(s).", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS3 are clearly based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) clearly leverage FS3\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) clearly support FS3\u2019s well-being and/or behavior to meet their math learning need(s).", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate plans adaptation(s) for FS3 to participate in the math lesson by creating a targeted, proactive plan** to support FS3\u2019s learning needs.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate\u2019s planning for FS3\u2019s adaptation(s) draws upon and/or refers to evidence- based practice(s) and/or research appropriate to FS3\u2019s well-being and/or behavior."], ["Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they maintain a safe, positive learning environment* during the math lesson. Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they use a UDL-focused strategy(ies) to support their students during the math lesson. Candidate provides a demonstration and/or description with 4 or more minor or a major inaccuracy(ies) in their math content instruction. Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of the math lesson described in Step 1.", "Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they maintain a safe, positive learning environment* during the math lesson. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they use a UDL-focused strategy(ies) to support their students during the math lesson. Candidate provides a demonstration and/or description with 3 or fewer minor inaccuracies in their math content instruction. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of the math lesson described in Step 1.", "Candidate provides a demonstration and description of how they clearly maintain a safe, positive learning environment* during the math lesson. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they use a UDL-focused strategy(ies) to support their students during the math lesson. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of accurate math content instruction. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of the math lesson described in Step 1.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate demonstrates and describes how they use multiple UDL-focused strategies to support their students during the math lesson.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate facilitates structured opportunities for the students to collaboratively explore the math content and practice through discussion, writing, and/or reading."], ["Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they engage the students in higher-order thinking to support student learning. Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they monitor and/or respond intentionally to support student learning.", "Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they engage the students in higher-order thinking to support student learning. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they monitor and/or respond intentionally to support student learning.", "Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they engage the students in higher-order thinking to support student learning. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they monitor and respond intentionally to support student learning.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate demonstrates and describes how they use multiple assessment(s) to monitor and adjust instruction to support student learning.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate demonstrates and describes how they connect math learning to real-life contexts to engage, motivate, and/or extend student learning."], ["Candidate does not reflect on what went well and/or what did not go well or as expected in the lesson. Candidate does not reflect on the impact of getting to know their students before teaching the lesson. Candidate does not reflect on the impact of the safe, positive environment they created to include all students. Candidate does not reflect on the impact of their asset-based approach. Candidate does not reflect on the impact of their UDL- focused strategy(ies). Candidate does not reflect on the impact of engaging students in higher-order thinking. Candidate does not analyze* student progress in meeting the math and/or ALD learning goals. Candidate does not analyze* the impact of the adaptation(s) used to support FS1, FS2, and/or FS3 in making progress toward meeting the learning goals.", "Candidate vaguely reflects on what went well and/or what did not go well or as expected in the lesson. Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of getting to know their students before teaching the lesson. Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of the safe, positive environment they created to include all students. Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of their asset-based approach. Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of their UDL- focused strategy(ies). Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of engaging students in higher-order thinking. Candidate vaguely analyzes* student progress in meeting the math and/or ALD learning goals. Candidate vaguely analyzes* the impact of the adaptation(s) used to support FS1, FS2, and/or FS3 in making progress toward meeting the learning goals.", "Candidate clearly reflects on what went well and what did not go well or as expected in the lesson. Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of getting to know their students before teaching the lesson. Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of the safe, positive environment they created to include all students. Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of their asset-based approach. Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of their UDL- focused strategy(ies). Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of engaging students in higher-order thinking. Candidate clearly analyzes* student progress in meeting the math and ALD learning goals. Candidate clearly analyzes* the impact of the adaptation(s) used to support FS1, FS2, and FS3 in making progress toward meeting the learning goals.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s reflection demonstrates an understanding that affirming, validating, and/or leveraging the students\u2019 assets and/or interests influence student math learning.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: When reflecting on the impact of their instruction, the candidate refers to specific examples from the teaching of their math lesson to determine which strategy(ies) moved learning forward."], ["Candidate\u2019s application of next steps does not describe what they learned throughout this cycle. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps does not describe how they would advance the math and/or ALD learning for the group. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps does not describe how they would continue to support the learning need(s) of FS1, FS2, and/or FS3. Candidate does not use a specific example(s) from Steps 1, 2, or 3 and/or does not justify their next instructional move for math learning, or the provided example does not justify the next instructional move for math learning.", "Candidate\u2019s application of next steps vaguely describes what they learned throughout this cycle. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps vaguely describes how they would advance the math and/or ALD learning for the group. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps vaguely describes how they would continue to support the learning need(s) of FS1, FS2, and/or FS3. Candidate uses an example(s) from Steps 1, 2, or 3 that vaguely justifies their next instructional move for math learning.", "Candidate\u2019s application of next steps clearly describes what they learned throughout this cycle. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps clearly describes how they would advance the math and ALD learning for the group. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps clearly describes how they would continue to support the learning need(s) of FS1, FS2, and FS3. Candidate uses a specific example(s) from Steps 1, 2, or 3 that clearly justifies their next instructional move for math learning.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s responses demonstrate how they will continue to leverage students\u2019 assets and/or interests in future lessons to support math learning.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate describes how they will apply what they have learned about the group and the focus students to plan future instruction that clearly reinforces, strengthens, and/or extends students\u2019 higher-order thinking related to math and ALD."]], "ms-literacy": [["Candidate does not use learning/assessment information to plan instruction. Candidate does not select a CA State* ELA/Literacy and/or ELD strands/standards for the unit plan OR selects strands/standards that are more than one grade level above or below the students they plan to teach in the unit plan. Candidate does not include foundational reading skill(s)** and/or an additional theme*** in their ELA/Literacy goal(s) for the unit plan. Candidate does not include an ELD goal, OR the ELD goal(s) are not grade-level appropriate, OR the ELD goal(s) do not support the ELA/Literacy learning goal(s) for the unit plan. Candidate does not plan formative assessments in each lesson, OR the formative assessments are not connected to the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning goal(s). Candidate does not plan a summative assessment OR plans a summative assessment that does not measure the students\u2019 progress in meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. The included rubric or performance criteria for the summative assessment do not measure the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate\u2019s planning has 4 or more minor errors or a major error when addressing foundational reading skill(s),** additional theme(s),*** and/or integrated ELD.", "Candidate vaguely uses information from recent learning/assessments or the information used to plan instruction is not recent. Candidate selects CA State* ELA/Literacy and ELD strands/standards that are either one grade level above or one grade level below the grade of the students they plan to teach in the unit plan. Candidate develops ELA/Literacy learning goal(s) that vaguely include foundational reading skill(s)** and/or an additional theme*** for the unit plan. Candidate develops ELD goal(s) that vaguely support the ELA/Literacy learning goal(s) for the unit plan. Candidate plans one or more formative assessment(s) in each lesson that vaguely connect to the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning goal(s). Candidate plans one summative assessment that vaguely measures the students\u2019 progress in meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate includes a rubric or performance criteria for the summative assessment that vaguely measure the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate\u2019s planning includes 3 or fewer minor errors when addressing foundational reading skill(s),** additional theme(s),*** and/or integrated ELD.", "Candidate clearly uses information from recent learning/assessments to plan instruction. Candidate selects grade-level appropriate CA State* ELA/Literacy and ELD strands/standards for the unit plan. Candidate develops grade-level appropriate ELA/Literacy learning goal(s) that include both foundational reading skill(s)** and additional theme(s)*** for the unit plan. Candidate develops grade-level appropriate ELD goal(s) that clearly support the ELA/Literacy learning goal(s) for the unit plan. Candidate plans one or more formative assessment(s) in each lesson that are clearly connected to the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning goal(s). Candidate plans one summative assessment that clearly measures the students\u2019 progress in meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate includes a rubric or performance criteria for the summative assessment that clearly measure the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate\u2019s planning accurately addresses foundational reading skill(s),** additional theme(s),*** and integrated ELD.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate plans multiple formative assessments within each lesson of the unit to monitor the group\u2019s ELA/Literacy and ELD understandings and learning needs.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus When developing the summative assessment and corresponding rubric or performance criteria, the candidate includes real-life scenarios that build upon the group\u2019s culture, language(s), and/or experiences."], ["In their planning, the candidate does not leverage student assets and/or interests. Candidate does not plan to use UDL strategy(ies) when teaching the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD content. The unit plan does not include three lessons or the lessons do not align and build upon one another to create a progression of learning. Candidate does not plan to teach foundational reading skill(s)* and/or does not plan to teach foundational reading skill(s) using a direct, systematic, and explicit approach. Candidate does not include an additional theme** and/or does not plan to actively engage the students while teaching the additional theme(s). Candidate\u2019s plan does not integrate ELD, and/or the ELD does not support the foundational reading skill(s)* and/or the additional theme(s).** Candidate does not include adaptation(s) that address the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests and/or learning needs.", "In their planning, the candidate vaguely leverages student assets and/or interests. Candidate vaguely plans to use UDL strategy(ies) when teaching the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD content. The unit plan includes three lessons that vaguely align and build upon one another to create a progression of learning. When planning to teach the foundational reading skill(s),* candidate vaguely includes a direct, systematic, and explicit approach. Candidate vaguely plans to engage the students with the additional theme(s).** Candidate\u2019s plan integrates ELD that vaguely supports the foundational reading skill(s)* or the additional theme(s).** Candidate includes adaptation(s) that vaguely address the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests and/or learning needs.", "In their planning, the candidate clearly leverages student assets and/or interests. Candidate clearly plans to use appropriate UDL strategy(ies) when teaching the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD content. The unit plan includes three lessons that clearly align and build upon one another to create a progression of learning. When planning to teach the foundational reading skill(s),* candidate clearly includes a direct, systematic, and explicit approach. Candidate clearly plans to actively engage the students with the additional theme(s).** Candidate\u2019s plan integrates ELD that clearly supports the foundational reading skill(s)* and the additional theme(s).** Candidate includes a plan for adaptation(s) that clearly address the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests and learning needs.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate leverages student assets by intentionally incorporating students\u2019 cultural backgrounds, lived experiences, interests, and/or primary languages into the lesson design.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Each of the candidate\u2019s lessons include multiple UDL strategies to support the group and the FS toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goal(s) based on their assets and/or interests and learning needs."], ["Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of how they teach the foundational reading skill(s) using a direct and explicit approach. Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of how they actively engage the students during the teaching of the foundational reading skill(s). Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of the literacy lesson(s) described in Step 1.", "Candidate includes an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they teach the foundational reading skill(s) using a direct and explicit approach. Candidate includes an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they actively engage the students during the teaching of the foundational reading skill(s). Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of the literacy lesson(s) described in Step 1.", "Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of how they teach the foundational reading skill(s) using a direct and explicit approach. Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of how they actively engage the students during the teaching of the foundational reading skill(s). Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of the literacy lesson(s) described in Step 1.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate models the targeted foundational reading skill(s) using precise academic language and think-alouds to make cognitive processes visible.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate formatively assesses students\u2019 foundational reading skill(s) throughout the lesson(s) and structures frequent opportunities for students to respond and receive feedback."], ["Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they leverage student assets and/or interests while teaching the additional theme(s)* from the ELA/ELD Framework. Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of how they actively engage students in learning the additional theme(s) from the ELA/ELD Framework.", "Candidate provides a vague demonstration and/or description of how they leverage student assets and/or interests while teaching the additional theme(s)* from the ELA/ELD Framework. Candidate provides a vague demonstration and/or description of how they actively engage students in learning the additional theme(s) from the ELA/ELD Framework.", "Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they leverage student assets and/or interests while teaching the additional theme(s)* from the ELA/ELD Framework. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they actively engage students in learning the additional theme(s) from the ELA/ELD Framework.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate incorporates students\u2019 cultural backgrounds, lived experiences, interests, and/or primary languages into instruction of the additional theme(s) from the ELA/ELD framework.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate provides structured opportunities for the students to collaboratively explore the additional theme(s) through discussion, writing, and/or reading."], ["Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of UDL strategy(ies). Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they integrate ELD to support the teaching of the foundational reading skill(s) and/or the additional theme(s).", "Candidate includes a vague demonstration and/or description of the UDL strategy(ies) they use to teach the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD content. Candidate provides a vague demonstration and/or description of how they integrate ELD to support the teaching of the foundational reading skill(s) and/or the additional theme(s).", "Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of the UDL strategy(ies) they use to teach the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD content. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they integrate ELD to support the teaching of the foundational reading skill(s) and/or the additional theme(s).", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of multiple UDL strategies used to support the teaching of the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning goals.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate encourages translanguaging as a resource to deepen comprehension and language transfer."], ["Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they use formative assessment(s) to monitor student progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals. Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of how they respond intentionally to formative assessment results to support student progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals.", "Candidate provides a vague demonstration and/or description of how they use formative assessment(s) to monitor student progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals. Candidate includes a vague demonstration and/or description of how they respond intentionally to formative assessment results to support student progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals.", "Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they use formative assessment(s) to monitor student progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals. Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of how they respond intentionally to formative assessment results to support student progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate uses multiple formative assessments, such as purposeful questioning, academic discussion, analysis of student work, and/or real-time checks for understanding, to monitor student learning in relation to both ELA/Literacy and ELD goals.", "All of Levels 3 and 4, plus: Candidate analyzes student responses during instruction to identify patterns and any misconceptions. Based on this evidence, the candidate immediately adapts instruction in meaningful ways, including differentiating tasks, providing targeted scaffolds, and/or extending the learning for the students."], ["Candidate\u2019s reflection does not include an analysis of the group\u2019s and/or the FS\u2019s summative assessment results. The candidate does not identify understandings and/or misconceptions related to the group\u2019s and/or the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD goals, OR the candidate does not base their analysis on the information they gathered while teaching and/or the summative assessment results. Candidate does not provide specific, actionable feedback for the FS, OR the specific, actionable feedback is not based on the summative assessment results. Candidate does not provide a description of the impact of their instructional approach(es) and/or their choice of student activity(ies) during the unit for the group, including the FS. Candidate does not provide an explanation of what instructional changes they would make for the group, including the FS, if they taught the unit again.", "Candidate\u2019s reflection includes a vague analysis of the group\u2019s and/or the FS\u2019s summative assessment results. Based on their analysis of the summative assessment results and the information gathered during their teaching, the candidate vaguely identifies understandings and/or misconceptions related to the group\u2019s and/or the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals. Candidate provides feedback to the FS that is vague, not actionable, or not clearly based on the student\u2019s performance on the summative assessment, OR the candidate provides developmentally inappropriate feedback. Candidate provides a vague description of the impact of their instructional approach(es) and/or their choice of student activity(ies) during the unit for the group, including the FS. Candidate provides a vague explanation of what instructional changes they would make for the group, including the FS, if they taught the unit again.", "Candidate\u2019s reflection includes a clear analysis of the group\u2019s and the FS\u2019s summative assessment results. Based on their analysis of the summative assessment results and the information gathered during their teaching, the candidate clearly identifies understandings and/or misconceptions related to the group\u2019s and the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD goals. Candidate provides specific, actionable feedback for the FS that is clearly based on the FS\u2019s performance on the summative assessment. Candidate provides a clear description of the impact of their instructional approach(es) and their choice of student activity(ies) during the unit for the group, including the FS. Candidate provides a clear explanation of what instructional changes they would make for the group, including the FS, if they taught the unit again.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s specific, actionable feedback for the FS is aligned to the learning goals of the unit. It clearly names what the FS did well and/or what needs improvement based on specific strengths and/or needs of the FS using concrete examples from the summative assessment and/or observations.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: When reflecting on the impact of their instruction, the candidate uses data from the unit plan, specific examples from their teaching or commentary, and data from formative and/or summative assessment(s) to determine which strategies moved learning forward."], ["Candidate does not include a plan for follow-up instruction for the FS, either re-teaching or extension, based on their analysis of the FS\u2019s performance during the unit, including summative assessment results. The video and commentary do not include either: \u2022 Re-Teach: A demonstration and/or description of the targeted intervention and/or individualized strategy used to support the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goal(s) OR \u2022 Extend: A demonstration and/or description of the instruction that deepens and/or advances the FS\u2019s ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning Candidate does not include specific example(s) from Steps 1, 2, and/or 3 to support their follow-up instructional decision making, OR evidence cited does not support follow- up instructional decisions.", "Candidate includes a vague plan for follow-up instruction for the FS, either re-teaching or extension, based on their analysis of the FS\u2019s performance during the unit, including summative assessment results. The video and/or commentary include either: \u2022 Re-Teach: An unclear demonstration and/or description of the targeted intervention and/or individualized strategy used to support the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goal(s) OR \u2022 Extend: An unclear demonstration and/or description of the instruction that deepens and/or advances the FS\u2019s ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning Candidate uses vague example(s) from Steps 1, 2, and/or 3 to support their follow-up instructional decision making.", "Candidate includes a clear plan for follow-up instruction for the FS, either re-teaching or extension, based on their analysis of the FS\u2019s performance during the unit, including summative assessment results. The video and commentary include either: \u2022 Re-Teach: A clear demonstration and description of the targeted intervention and/or individualized strategy used to support the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goal(s) OR \u2022 Extend: A clear demonstration and description of the instruction that deepens and/or advances the FS\u2019s ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning Candidate clearly uses specific example(s) from Steps 1, 2, and/or 3 to support their follow-up instructional decision making.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate leverages the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests by intentionally incorporating the student\u2019s cultural, linguistic, and/or lived experiences into the follow-up instruction design.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate synthesizes multiple sources of evidence from Steps 1, 2, and 3 to justify their instructional decisions and clearly explains how the selected strategy accelerates the FS\u2019s learning of the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD content."]], "ss-c1": [["Candidate does not use information from recent content- specific learning* to plan instruction. Candidate does not select a grade-level appropriate CA State content-specific Strand/Standard and/or Curriculum Framework or they select a strand/ standard that is more than one grade level above or below the students they plan to teach. Candidate does not develop a content-specific learning goal that is based on the selected content strand/standard. Candidate does not develop an ALD learning goal or the ALD learning goal does not align with the content-specific learning goal. Candidate does not describe how they will create a safe, positive learning environment or does not describe how the environment will support students during the content- specific lesson. Candidate does not describe how they will leverage the students\u2019 assets and/or interests. Candidate does not describe how they will engage students in higher-order thinking** to deepen their content-specific understanding. Candidate does not describe how they will monitor student learning during the content- specific lesson. Candidate does not describe how they will use UDL-focused instructional strategy(ies) to support student learning.", "Candidate vaguely uses information from recent content- specific learning* to plan instruction. Candidate selects a grade-level appropriate CA State content- specific Strand/Standard and/or Curriculum Framework that is either one grade level above or below the students they plan to teach. Candidate develops a content- specific learning goal that is vaguely based on the selected content strand/standard. Candidate develops an ALD learning goal that vaguely aligns with the content-specific learning goal. Candidate vaguely describes how they will create a safe, positive learning environment or vaguely describes how the learning environment will support students during the content- specific lesson. Candidate vaguely describes how they will leverage the students\u2019 assets and/or interests. Candidate vaguely describes how they will engage students in higher-order thinking** to deepen their content-specific understanding. Candidate vaguely describes how they will monitor student learning during the content- specific lesson. Candidate vaguely describes how they will use UDL-focused instructional strategy(ies) to support student learning.", "Candidate clearly uses information from recent content- specific learning* to plan instruction. Candidate selects a grade-level appropriate CA State content- specific Strand/Standard and/or Curriculum Framework for the students they plan to teach. Candidate develops a content- specific learning goal that is clearly based on the selected content strand/standard. Candidate develops an ALD learning goal that clearly aligns with the content-specific learning goal. Candidate describes how they will create a safe, positive learning environment that clearly supports students during the content-specific lesson. Candidate clearly describes how they will leverage the students\u2019 assets and/or interests. Candidate clearly describes how they will engage students in higher-order thinking** to deepen their content-specific understanding. Candidate clearly describes how they will monitor student learning during the content- specific lesson. Candidate clearly describes how they will use UDL-focused instructional strategy(ies) to support student learning.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s planning clearly includes opportunities for students to learn collaboratively to progress toward the content- specific and related content- specific ALD learning goals.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate designs a lesson that reflects the interconnectedness of the content-specific area plus an additional academic content area (e.g., literacy, social science, art, science, PE)."], ["Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS1 are not based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) do not leverage FS1\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) do not support FS1\u2019s ALD learning need(s) through reading, writing, listening, and/or speaking.", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS1 are vaguely based on recent learning* or information used is not recent. Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) vaguely leverage FS1\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) vaguely support FS1\u2019s ALD learning need(s) through reading, writing, listening, and/or speaking.", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS1 are clearly based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) clearly leverage FS1\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) clearly support FS1\u2019s ALD learning need(s) through reading, writing, listening, and/or speaking.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate plans adaptation(s) for FS1 to participate in the content-specific lesson by using multiple modes of communication** to support FS1\u2019s learning needs.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate\u2019s planning for FS1\u2019s adaptation(s) draws upon and/or refers to evidence- based practice(s) and/or research appropriate to FS1\u2019s ALD."], ["Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS2 are not based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) do not leverage FS2\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) do not support FS2\u2019s content- specific learning need(s).**", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS2 are vaguely based on recent learning* or information used is not recent. Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) vaguely leverage FS2\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) vaguely support FS2\u2019s content- specific learning need(s).**", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS2 are clearly based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) clearly leverage FS2\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) clearly support FS2\u2019s content- specific learning need(s).**", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate plans adaptation(s) for FS2 to participate in the content-specific lesson by using two or more multisensory strategies*** to support FS2\u2019s learning needs.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate\u2019s planning for FS2\u2019s adaptation(s) draws upon and/or refers to evidence- based content-specific practice(s) and/or research appropriate to FS2\u2019s content- specific learning need(s)."], ["Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS3 are not based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) do not leverage FS3\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) do not support FS3\u2019s well-being and/or behavior to meet their content-specific learning need(s).", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS3 are vaguely based on recent learning* or information used is not recent. Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) vaguely leverage FS3\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) vaguely support FS3\u2019s well- being and/or behavior to meet their content-specific learning need(s).", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for FS3 are clearly based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) clearly leverage FS3\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned content- specific lesson adaptation(s) clearly support FS3\u2019s well-being and/or behavior to meet their content-specific learning need(s).", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate plans adaptation(s) for FS3 to participate in the content-specific lesson by creating a targeted, proactive plan** to support FS3\u2019s learning needs.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate\u2019s planning for FS3\u2019s adaptation(s) draws upon and/or refers to evidence- based practice(s) and/or research appropriate to FS3\u2019s well-being and/or behavior."], ["Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they maintain a safe, positive learning environment* during the content-specific lesson. Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they use a UDL-focused strategy(ies) to support their students during the content-specific lesson. Candidate provides a demonstration and/or description with 4 or more minor or a major inaccuracy(ies) in their content- specific instruction. Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of the content- specific lesson described in Step 1.", "Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they maintain a safe, positive learning environment* during the content-specific lesson. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they use a UDL-focused strategy(ies) to support their students during the content-specific lesson. Candidate provides a demonstration and/or description with 3 or fewer minor inaccuracies in their content-specific instruction. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of the content- specific lesson described in Step 1.", "Candidate provides a demonstration and description of how they clearly maintain a safe, positive learning environment* during the content-specific lesson. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they use a UDL-focused strategy(ies) to support their students during the content- specific lesson. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of accurate content-specific instruction. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of the content-specific lesson described in Step 1.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate demonstrates and describes how they use multiple UDL-focused strategies to support their students during the content- specific lesson.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate facilitates structured opportunities for the students to collaboratively explore the content-specific material through discussion, writing, and/or reading."], ["Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they engage the students in higher-order thinking to support student learning. Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they monitor and/or respond intentionally to support student learning.", "Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they engage the students in higher-order thinking to support student learning. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they monitor and/or respond intentionally to support student learning.", "Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they engage the students in higher-order thinking to support student learning. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they monitor and respond intentionally to support student learning.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate demonstrates and describes how they use multiple assessment(s) to monitor and adjust instruction to support student learning.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate demonstrates and describes how they connect content-specific learning to real-life contexts to engage, motivate, and/or extend student learning."], ["Candidate does not reflect on what went well and/or what did not go well or as expected in the lesson. Candidate does not reflect on the impact of getting to know their students before teaching the lesson. Candidate does not reflect on the impact of the safe, positive environment they created to include all students. Candidate does not reflect on the impact of their asset-based approach. Candidate does not reflect on the impact of their UDL- focused strategy(ies). Candidate does not reflect on the impact of engaging students in higher-order thinking. Candidate does not analyze* student progress in meeting the content-specific and/or ALD learning goals. Candidate does not analyze* the impact of the adaptation(s) used to support FS1, FS2, and/or FS3 in making progress toward meeting the learning goals.", "Candidate vaguely reflects on what went well and/or what did not go well or as expected in the lesson. Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of getting to know their students before teaching the lesson. Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of the safe, positive environment they created to include all students. Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of their asset-based approach. Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of their UDL- focused strategy(ies). Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of engaging students in higher-order thinking. Candidate vaguely analyzes* student progress in meeting the content-specific and/or ALD learning goals. Candidate vaguely analyzes* the impact of the adaptation(s) used to support FS1, FS2, and/or FS3 in making progress toward meeting the learning goals.", "Candidate clearly reflects on what went well and what did not go well or as expected in the lesson. Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of getting to know their students before teaching the lesson. Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of the safe, positive environment they created to include all students. Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of their asset-based approach. Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of their UDL- focused strategy(ies). Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of engaging students in higher-order thinking. Candidate clearly analyzes* student progress in meeting the content-specific and ALD learning goals. Candidate clearly analyzes* the impact of the adaptation(s) used to support FS1, FS2, and FS3 in making progress toward meeting the learning goals.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s reflection demonstrates an understanding that affirming, validating, and/or leveraging the students\u2019 assets and/or interests influence student content-specific learning.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: When reflecting on the impact of their instruction, the candidate refers to specific examples from the teaching of their content-specific lesson to determine which strategy(ies) moved learning forward."], ["Candidate\u2019s application of next steps does not describe what they learned throughout this cycle. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps does not describe how they would advance the content-specific and/or ALD learning for the group. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps does not describe how they would continue to support the learning need(s) of FS1, FS2, and/or FS3. Candidate does not use a specific example(s) from Steps 1, 2, or 3 and/or does not justify their next instructional move for content-specific learning, or the provided example does not justify the next instructional move for content-specific learning.", "Candidate\u2019s application of next steps vaguely describes what they learned throughout this cycle. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps vaguely describes how they would advance the content-specific and/or ALD learning for the group. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps vaguely describes how they would continue to support the learning need(s) of FS1, FS2, and/or FS3. Candidate uses an example(s) from Steps 1, 2, or 3 that vaguely justifies their next instructional move for content- specific learning.", "Candidate's application of next steps clearly describes what they learned throughout this cycle. Candidate's application of next steps clearly describes how they would advance the content-specific and ALD learning for the group. Candidate's application of next steps clearly describes how they would continue to support the learning need(s) of FS1, FS2, and FS3. Candidate uses a specific example(s) from Steps 1, 2, or 3 that clearly justifies their next instructional move for content- specific learning.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s responses demonstrate how they will continue to leverage students\u2019 assets and/or interests in future lessons to support content-specific learning.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate describes how they will apply what they have learned about the group and the focus students to plan future instruction that clearly reinforces, strengthens, and/or extends students\u2019 higher-order thinking related to content- specific and ALD learning."]], "ss-c2": [["Candidate does not use learning/assessment information to plan instruction. Candidate does not select a content-specific CA State standard(s) and/or framework(s) and/or ELD standard(s) for the unit plan OR selects standards that are more than one grade level above or below the students they plan to teach in the unit plan. Candidate does not include a content-specific goal for the unit plan. Candidate does not include an ELD goal, OR the ELD goal(s) are not grade-level appropriate, OR the ELD goal(s) do not support the content-specific learning goal(s) for the unit plan. Candidate does not plan formative assessments in each lesson, OR the formative assessments are not connected to the content-specific and/or ELD learning goal(s) of the unit plan. Candidate does not plan a summative assessment OR plans a summative assessment that does not measure the students\u2019 progress in meeting the content- specific and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate does not include a rubric or performance criteria, OR the included rubric or performance criteria for the summative assessment do not measure the content-specific and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate\u2019s planning has 4 or more minor errors or a major error.", "Candidate vaguely uses information from recent learning/assessments* or the information used to plan instruction is not recent. Candidate selects content-specific, CA State standard(s) and/or framework(s) and ELD standard(s) that are either one grade level above or one grade level below the grade of the students they plan to teach in the unit plan. Candidate develops a content- specific learning goal(s) that is not grade-level appropriate for the unit plan. Candidate develops ELD goal(s) that vaguely support the content- specific learning goal(s) for the unit plan. Candidate plans one or more formative assessment(s) in each lesson that vaguely connect to the content-specific and/or ELD learning goal(s) of the unit plan. Candidate plans one summative assessment that vaguely measures the students\u2019 progress in meeting the content-specific and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate includes a rubric or performance criteria for the summative assessment that vaguely measure the content- specific and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate\u2019s planning includes 3 or fewer minor errors.", "Candidate clearly uses information from recent learning/assessments* to plan instruction. Candidate selects grade-level appropriate content-specific CA State standard(s) and/or framework(s) and ELD standard(s) for the unit plan. Candidate develops grade-level appropriate content-specific learning goal(s) for the unit plan. Candidate develops grade-level appropriate ELD goal(s) that clearly support the content-specific learning goal(s) for the unit plan. Candidate plans one or more formative assessment(s) in each lesson that are clearly connected to the content-specific and/or ELD learning goal(s) of the unit plan. Candidate plans one summative assessment that clearly measures the students\u2019 progress in meeting the content-specific and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate includes a rubric or performance criteria for the summative assessment that clearly measure the content-specific and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate\u2019s planning is accurate.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate plans multiple formative assessments within each lesson of the unit to monitor the group\u2019s content-specific and ELD understandings and learning needs.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus When developing the summative assessment and corresponding rubric or performance criteria, the candidate includes real-life scenarios that build upon the group\u2019s culture, language(s), and/or experiences."], ["In their planning, the candidate does not leverage student assets and/or interests. Candidate does not plan to use UDL strategy(ies) when teaching the content-specific and/or ELD content. The unit plan does not include three lessons or the lessons do not align and build upon one another to create a progression of learning. Candidate does not plan active, engaging content-specific instruction. Candidate\u2019s plan does not integrate ELD, and/or the ELD does not support content- specific learning. Candidate does not include adaptation(s) that address the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests and/or learning needs.", "In their planning, the candidate vaguely leverages student assets and/or interests. Candidate vaguely plans to use UDL strategy(ies) when teaching the content-specific and/or ELD content. The unit plan includes three lessons that vaguely align and build upon one another to create a progression of learning. Candidate vaguely plans active, engaging content-specific instruction. Candidate plans to integrate ELD that vaguely supports content-specific learning. Candidate includes adaptation(s) that vaguely address the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests and/or learning needs.", "In their planning, the candidate clearly leverages student assets and/or interests. Candidate clearly plans to use appropriate UDL strategy(ies) when teaching the content- specific and/or ELD content. The unit plan includes three lessons that clearly align and build upon one another to create a progression of learning. Candidate clearly plans active, engaging content-specific instruction. Candidate plans to integrate ELD that clearly supports content-specific learning. Candidate includes a plan for adaptation(s) that clearly address the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests and learning needs.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate leverages student assets by intentionally incorporating students\u2019 cultural backgrounds, lived experiences, interests, and/or primary languages into the lesson design.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Each of the candidate\u2019s lessons include multiple UDL strategies to intentionally support the group and the FS based on their assets and/or interests and learning needs."], ["Candidate does not demonstrate and/or describe how they engage students in deep learning of the content to enhance the students\u2019 content- specific knowledge, skills, and/or abilities. Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of the content- specific lesson(s) described in Step 1.", "Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or describes how they engage students in deep learning of the content to enhance the students\u2019 content-specific knowledge, skills, and/or abilities. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of the content- specific lesson(s) described in Step 1.", "Candidate clearly demonstrates and describes how they engage students in deep learning of the content to enhance the students\u2019 content-specific knowledge, skills, and/or abilities. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of the content-specific lesson(s) described in Step 1.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate is responsive to students\u2019 age, language, and/or content-specific development to deepen and/or advance students\u2019 knowledge related to the content.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate demonstrates and describes how they intentionally design and implement learning experiences that deeply engage students in the content."], ["Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they leverage student assets and/or interests while teaching the content-specific and/or ELD content. Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of the UDL strategy(ies) they use to teach the content-specific and/or ELD content. Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of how they actively engage the students during the content-specific and/or ELD learning.", "Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they leverage student assets and/or interests while teaching the content-specific and/or ELD content. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of the UDL strategy(ies) they use to teach the content-specific and/or ELD content. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they actively engage the students during the content-specific and/or ELD learning.", "Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they leverage student assets and/or interests while teaching the content-specific and/or ELD content. Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of the UDL strategy(ies) they use to teach the content- specific and/or ELD content. Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of how they actively engage the students during the content- specific and/or ELD learning.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate incorporates the students\u2019 cultural backgrounds, lived experiences, interests, and/or primary languages into the content-specific instruction.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of multiple UDL strategies used to support the teaching of the content-specific and ELD learning goals that address the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests and learning needs."], ["Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of how they integrate ELD to support the content-specific instruction.", "Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they integrate ELD to support the content-specific instruction.", "Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they integrate ELD to support the content-specific instruction.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate purposefully leverages students\u2019 assets and/or interests and explains why this instructional approach supports students in progressing toward meeting the content-specific and ELD goals.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate encourages translanguaging as a resource to deepen comprehension and language transfer."], ["Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they use formative assessment(s) to monitor student progress toward meeting the content- specific and/or ELD goals. Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of how they respond intentionally to formative assessment results to support student progress toward meeting the content- specific and/or ELD goals.", "Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they use formative assessment(s) to monitor student progress toward meeting the content- specific and/or ELD goals. Candidate includes an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they respond intentionally to formative assessment results to support student progress toward meeting the content- specific and/or ELD goals.", "Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they use formative assessment(s) to monitor student progress toward meeting the content-specific and/or ELD goals. Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of how they respond intentionally to formative assessment results to support student progress toward meeting the content-specific and/or ELD goals.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate uses multiple formative assessments, such as purposeful questioning, academic discussion, analysis of student work, and/or real-time checks for understanding, to monitor student learning in relation to both content- specific and ELD goals.", "All of Levels 3 and 4, plus: Candidate analyzes student responses during instruction to identify patterns and any misconceptions. Based on this evidence, the candidate immediately adapts instruction in meaningful ways, including differentiating tasks, providing targeted scaffolds, and/or extending the learning for the students."], ["Candidate\u2019s reflection does not include an analysis of the group\u2019s and/or the FS\u2019s summative assessment results. Candidate does not identify understandings and/or misconceptions related to the group\u2019s and/or the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the content-specific and ELD goals, OR the candidate does not base their analysis on the information they gathered while teaching and/or the summative assessment results. Candidate does not provide specific, actionable feedback for the FS, OR the specific, actionable feedback is not based on the summative assessment results. Candidate does not provide a description of the impact of their instructional approach(es) and/or their choice of student activity(ies) during the unit for the group, including the FS. Candidate does not provide an explanation of what instructional changes they would make for the group, including the FS, if they taught the unit again.", "Candidate\u2019s reflection includes a vague analysis of the group\u2019s and/or the FS\u2019s summative assessment results. Based on their analysis of the summative assessment results and the information gathered during their teaching, the candidate vaguely identifies understandings and/or misconceptions related to the group\u2019s and/or the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the content-specific and/or ELD goals. Candidate provides feedback to the FS that is vague, not actionable, or not clearly based on the student\u2019s performance on the summative assessment. Candidate provides a vague description of the impact of their instructional approach(es) and/or their choice of student activity(ies) during the unit for the group, including the FS. Candidate provides a vague explanation of what instructional changes they would make for the group, including the FS, if they taught the unit again.", "Candidate\u2019s reflection includes a clear analysis of the group\u2019s and the FS\u2019s summative assessment results. Based on their analysis of the summative assessment results and the information gathered during their teaching, the candidate clearly identifies understandings and/or misconceptions related to the group\u2019s and the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the content- specific and ELD goals. Candidate provides specific, actionable feedback for the FS that is clearly based on the FS\u2019s performance on the summative assessment. Candidate provides a clear description of the impact of their instructional approach(es) and their choice of student activity(ies) during the unit for the group, including the FS. Candidate provides a clear explanation of what instructional changes they would make for the group, including the FS, if they taught the unit again.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s specific, actionable feedback for the FS is aligned to the learning goals of the unit. It clearly names what the FS did well and/or what needs improvement based on specific strengths and/or needs of the FS using concrete examples from the summative assessment and/or observations.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: When reflecting on the impact of their instruction, the candidate uses data from the unit plan, specific examples from their teaching or commentary, and data from formative and/or summative assessment(s) to determine which strategies moved learning forward."], ["Candidate does not include a plan for follow-up instruction for the FS, either re-teaching or extension, based on their analysis of the FS\u2019s performance during the unit, including summative assessment results. The video and commentary do not include either: \u2022 Re-Teach: A demonstration and/or description of the targeted intervention and/or individualized strategy used to support the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the content- specific and/or ELD learning goal(s) OR \u2022 Extend: A demonstration and/or description of the instruction that deepens and/or advances the FS\u2019s content-specific and/or ELD learning Candidate does not include specific example(s) from Steps 1, 2, and/or 3 to support their follow-up instructional decision making, OR evidence cited does not support follow-up instructional decisions.", "Candidate includes a vague plan for follow-up instruction for the FS, either re-teaching or extension, based on their analysis of the FS\u2019s performance during the unit, including summative assessment results. The video and/or commentary include either: \u2022 Re-Teach: An unclear demonstration and/or description of the targeted intervention and/or individualized strategy used to support the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the content- specific and/or ELD learning goal(s) OR \u2022 Extend: An unclear demonstration and/or description of the instruction that deepens and/or advances the FS\u2019s content- specific and/or ELD learning Candidate uses vague example(s) from Steps 1, 2, and/or 3 to support their follow-up instructional decision making.", "Candidate includes a clear plan for follow-up instruction for the FS, either re-teaching or extension, based on their analysis of the FS\u2019s performance during the unit, including summative assessment results. The video and commentary include either: \u2022 Re-Teach: A clear demonstration and description of the targeted intervention and/or individualized strategy used to support the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the content-specific and/or ELD learning goal(s) OR \u2022 Extend: A clear demonstration and description of the instruction that deepens and/or advances the FS\u2019s content-specific and/or ELD learning Candidate clearly uses specific example(s) from Steps 1, 2, and/or 3 to support their follow-up instructional decision making.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate leverages the FS\u2019s assets by intentionally incorporating the student\u2019s cultural, linguistic, and/or lived experiences into the follow-up instruction design.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate synthesizes multiple sources of evidence from Steps 1, 2, and 3 to justify their instructional decisions and clearly explains how the selected strategy accelerates the FS\u2019s learning of the content-specific and/or ELD content."]], "mmsn-math": [["Candidate does not select an age-/grade-level appropriate CA State Math Content Strand/Standard or developmentally appropriate Core Content Connector (CCC)** and/or a Math Practice Standard or they select a strand/standard that is more than one grade level above or below the FS they plan to teach. Candidate does not develop a math learning goal*** that is based on the selected math strand/standard or CCC and/or does not include math content and/or practice. Candidate does not develop a math ALD learning goal or the ALD learning goal does not align with the math learning goal.*** Candidate does not describe how the lesson will support the FS\u2019s math-related IEP goal(s).*", "Candidate selects an age-/ grade-level appropriate CA State Math Content Strand/Standard or developmentally appropriate Core Content Connector (CCC)** and/or a Math Practice Standard that are either one grade level above or below the FS they plan to teach. Candidate develops a math learning goal*** that is vaguely based on the selected math strand/standard or CCC and includes math content and practice. Candidate develops a math ALD learning goal that vaguely aligns with the math learning goal.*** Candidate vaguely describes how the lesson will support the FS\u2019s math-related IEP goal(s).*", "Candidate selects an age-/ grade-level appropriate CA State Math Content Strand/Standard or developmentally appropriate Core Content Connector (CCC)** and a Math Practice Standard for the FS they plan to teach. Candidate develops a math learning goal*** that is clearly based on the selected math strand/standard or CCC and includes both math content and practice. Candidate develops a math ALD learning goal that clearly aligns with the math learning goal.*** Candidate clearly describes how the lesson will support the FS\u2019s math-related IEP goal(s).*", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s planning clearly includes opportunities for the FS to learn collaboratively to progress toward the math content and practice and math ALD learning goals.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate designs a math lesson that reflects the interconnectedness of math plus an additional academic content area (e.g., literacy, social science, art, science, PE)."], ["Candidate does not use information from recent math learning* and/or math-related IEP goal(s) to plan instruction. Candidate does not describe how they will engage the FS in UDL-focused instructional strategy(ies). Candidate does not describe how they will engage the FS in age and/or developmentally appropriate higher-order thinking to deepen their math understanding. Candidate does not describe how they will create a safe, positive learning environment** or does not describe how the environment will support the FS during the math lesson.", "Candidate vaguely uses information from recent math learning* and/or math-related IEP goal(s) to plan instruction. Candidate vaguely describes how they will engage the FS in UDL-focused instructional strategy(ies). Candidate vaguely describes how they will engage the FS in age and/or developmentally appropriate higher-order thinking to deepen their math understanding. Candidate vaguely describes how they will create a safe, positive learning environment** or vaguely describes how the learning environment will support the FS during the math lesson.", "Candidate clearly uses information from recent math learning* and math-related IEP goal(s) to plan instruction. Candidate clearly describes how they will engage the FS in UDL-focused instructional strategy(ies). Candidate clearly describes how they will engage the FS in age and/or developmentally appropriate higher-order thinking to deepen their math understanding. Candidate clearly describes how they will create a safe, positive learning environment** that supports the FS during the math lesson.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate plans for a safe, positive environment that considers the organization of space, time, and/or materials to support the learning needs of the FS during the math lesson.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate intentionally incorporates functionally appropriate skills with math learning to increase the FS's independence in real-world environments."], ["Candidate does not describe how they will monitor the FS\u2019s learning during the math lesson. Candidate does not describe how they will collaborate with and/or facilitate instructional support personnel to either: \u2022 provide individualized instruction to the FS during the math lesson OR \u2022 support the daily routines, activities, instruction, and/or intervention activities of other students while the candidate facilitates the math lesson.", "Candidate vaguely describes how they will monitor the FS\u2019s learning during the math lesson. Candidate vaguely describes how they will collaborate with and/or facilitate instructional support personnel to either: \u2022 provide individualized instruction to the FS during the math lesson OR \u2022 support the daily routines, activities, instruction, and/or intervention activities of other students while the candidate facilitates the math lesson.", "Candidate clearly describes how they will monitor the FS\u2019s learning during the math lesson. Candidate clearly describes how they will collaborate with and/or facilitate instructional support personnel to either: \u2022 provide individualized instruction to the FS during the math lesson OR \u2022 support the daily routines, activities, instruction, and/or intervention activities of other students while the candidate facilitates the math lesson.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s lesson plan demonstrates a purposeful integration of the instructional support personnel into the classroom environment, activities, and routines to maximize the FS\u2019s learning.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate collaborates with their cooperating teacher/mentor, instructional support personnel, and/or parents/guardians to identify the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests to plan a math lesson that engages the FS across routines, activities, and/or environments."], ["Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for the FS are not based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s)** do not leverage the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) do not support the FS\u2019s math and/or ALD learning need(s). Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) do not support the FS\u2019s math-related IEP goal(s).\u2020", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for the FS are vaguely based on recent learning* or information used is not recent. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s)** vaguely leverage the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) vaguely support the FS\u2019s math and/or ALD learning need(s). Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) vaguely support the FS\u2019s math-related IEP goal(s).\u2020", "Candidate\u2019s planned adaptation(s) for the FS are clearly based on recent learning.* Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s)** clearly leverage the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) clearly support the FS\u2019s math and ALD learning need(s). Candidate\u2019s planned math lesson adaptation(s) clearly support the FS\u2019s math-related IEP goal(s).\u2020", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate plans adaptation(s) for the FS to participate in the math lesson by using two or more multisensory strategies\u2021 to support the FS\u2019s learning needs.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate\u2019s planning for the FS's adaptation(s) draw upon and/or refer to evidence-based math practice(s) and/or research appropriate to the FS\u2019s math learning need(s)."], ["Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they maintain a safe, positive learning environment* during the math lesson. Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they use a UDL-focused strategy(ies) to support the FS during the math lesson. Candidate provides a demonstration and/or description with 4 or more minor or a major inaccuracy(ies) in their math content instruction. Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of the math lesson described in Step 1.", "Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they maintain a safe, positive learning environment* during the math lesson. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they use a UDL-focused strategy(ies) to support the FS during the math lesson. Candidate provides a demonstration and/or description with 3 or fewer minor inaccuracies in their math content instruction. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of the math lesson described in Step 1.", "Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they maintain a safe, positive learning environment* during the math lesson. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they use a UDL-focused strategy(ies) to support the FS during the math lesson. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of accurate math content instruction. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of the math lesson described in Step 1.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate demonstrates and describes how they use multiple UDL-focused strategies to support the FS during the math lesson.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate intentionally demonstrates and describes how they leverage the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests during the math lesson."], ["Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they engage the FS in developmentally appropriate higher-order thinking during the math lesson. Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they monitor and/or respond intentionally to support the FS\u2019s learning during the math lesson.", "Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they engage the FS in developmentally appropriate higher-order thinking during the math lesson. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they monitor and/or respond intentionally to support the FS\u2019s learning during the math lesson.", "Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they engage the FS in developmentally appropriate higher-order thinking during the math lesson. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they monitor and respond intentionally to support the FS\u2019s learning during the math lesson.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate demonstrates and describes how they use multiple assessment(s) to monitor and adjust instruction to support the FS\u2019s learning.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate demonstrates and describes how they connect math learning to real-life contexts to engage, motivate, and/or extend the FS\u2019s learning."], ["Candidate does not reflect on what went well and/or what did not go well or as expected in the lesson. Candidate does not reflect on the impact of getting to know the FS before teaching the lesson. Candidate does not reflect on the impact of the safe, positive environment they created. Candidate does not reflect on the impact of their asset-based approach. Candidate does not reflect on the impact of their UDL- focused strategy(ies). Candidate does not reflect on the impact of engaging the FS in higher-order thinking. Candidate does not analyze* the FS\u2019s progress in meeting the math and/or ALD learning goals. Candidate does not analyze* the impact of the adaptation(s) used to support the FS in making progress toward meeting the learning goals.", "Candidate vaguely reflects on what went well and/or what did not go well or as expected in the lesson. Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of getting to know the FS before teaching the lesson. Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of the safe, positive environment they created. Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of their asset-based approach. Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of their UDL- focused strategy(ies). Candidate vaguely reflects on the impact of engaging the FS in higher-order thinking. Candidate vaguely analyzes* the FS\u2019s progress in meeting the math and/or ALD learning goals. Candidate vaguely analyzes* the impact of the adaptation(s) used to support the FS in making progress toward meeting the learning goals.", "Candidate clearly reflects on what went well and what did not go well or as expected in the lesson. Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of getting to know the FS before teaching the lesson. Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of the safe, positive environment they created. Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of their asset-based approach. Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of their UDL- focused strategy(ies). Candidate clearly reflects on the impact of engaging the FS in higher-order thinking. Candidate clearly analyzes* the FS\u2019s progress in meeting the math and ALD learning goals. Candidate clearly analyzes* the impact of the adaptation(s) used to support the FS in making progress toward meeting the learning goals.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s reflection demonstrates an understanding that affirming, validating, and/or leveraging the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests influence math learning.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: When reflecting on the impact of their instruction, the candidate refers to specific examples from the teaching of their math lesson to determine which strategy(ies) moved learning forward."], ["Candidate\u2019s application of next steps does not describe what they learned throughout this cycle. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps does not describe how they would advance the FS\u2019s math and/or ALD learning. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps does not describe how they would continue to support the FS\u2019s learning need(s). Candidate\u2019s application of next steps does not describe how they would continue to collaborate with and/or facilitate instructional support personnel to support the FS in future instruction. Candidate does not use a specific example(s) from Steps 1, 2, or 3 and/or does not justify their next instructional move for math learning, or the provided example does not justify the next instructional move for math learning.", "Candidate\u2019s application of next steps vaguely describes what they learned throughout this cycle. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps vaguely describes how they would advance the FS\u2019s math and/or ALD learning. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps vaguely describes how they would continue to support the FS\u2019s learning need(s). Candidate\u2019s application of next steps vaguely describes how they would continue to collaborate with and/or facilitate instructional support personnel to support the FS in future instruction. Candidate uses an example(s) from Steps 1, 2, or 3 that vaguely justifies their next instructional move for math learning.", "Candidate\u2019s application of next steps clearly describes what they learned throughout this cycle. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps clearly describes how they would advance the FS\u2019s math and ALD learning. Candidate\u2019s application of next steps clearly describes how they would continue to support the FS\u2019s learning need(s). Candidate\u2019s application of next steps clearly describes how they would continue to collaborate with and/or facilitate instructional support personnel to support the FS in future instruction. Candidate uses a specific example(s) from Steps 1, 2, or 3 that clearly justifies their next instructional move for math learning.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s responses demonstrate how they will continue to leverage the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests in future lessons to support math learning.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate describes how they will apply what they have learned about the FS to plan future instruction that clearly reinforces, strengthens, and/or extends their higher-order thinking related to math and ALD."]], "mmsn-literacy": [["Candidate does not use recent learning/assessment and/or the FS\u2019s IEP information to plan instruction. Candidate does not select a CA State* ELA/Literacy strand/standard or developmentally appropriate CCCs** and/or ELD strands/standards for the unit plan OR selects CA State ELA/Literacy strands/standards or developmentally appropriate CCCs and/or ELD strands/standards that are more than one grade level above or below the FS they plan to teach in the unit plan. Candidate does not include foundational reading skill(s)\u2020 and/or an additional theme\u2021 in their ELA/Literacy goal(s), OR the ELA/Literacy learning goal(s) are not developmentally appropriate for the unit plan. Candidate does not include an ELD goal, OR the ELD goal(s) are not developmentally appropriate, OR the ELD goal(s) do not support the ELA/Literacy learning goal(s) for the unit plan. Candidate does not plan formative assessments in each lesson, OR the formative assessments are not connected to the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning goal(s). Candidate does not plan a summative assessment OR plans a summative assessment that does not measure the FS\u2019s progress in meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. The included rubric or performance criteria for the summative assessment do not measure the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate\u2019s planning has 4 or more minor errors or a major error when addressing foundational reading skill(s),\u2020 additional theme(s),\u2021 and/or integrated ELD.", "Candidate vaguely uses information from recent learning/assessments and/or the FS\u2019s IEP, OR the information used to plan instruction is not recent. Candidate selects CA State* ELA/Literacy strands/standards or developmentally appropriate CCCs** and ELD strands/standards that are either one grade level above or one grade level below the grade of the FS they plan to teach in the unit plan. Candidate creates ELA/Literacy learning goal(s) that vaguely include foundational reading skill(s)\u2020 and/or an additional theme\u2021 for the unit plan. Candidate creates ELD goal(s) that vaguely support the ELA/Literacy learning goal(s) for the unit plan. Candidate plans one or more formative assessment(s) in each lesson that vaguely connect to the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning goal(s). Candidate plans one summative assessment that vaguely measures the FS\u2019s progress in meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate includes a rubric or performance criteria for the summative assessment that vaguely measure the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate\u2019s planning includes 3 or fewer minor errors when addressing foundational reading skill(s),\u2020 additional theme(s),\u2021 and/or integrated ELD.", "Candidate clearly uses information from recent learning/assessments and the FS\u2019s IEP to plan instruction. Candidate selects grade-level appropriate CA State* ELA/Literacy strands/standards or developmentally appropriate CCCs** and ELD strands/standards for the unit plan. Candidate creates developmentally appropriate ELA/Literacy learning goal(s) that include both foundational reading skill(s)\u2020 and additional theme(s)\u2021 for the unit plan. Candidate creates developmentally appropriate ELD goal(s) that clearly support the ELA/Literacy learning goal(s) for the unit plan. Candidate plans one or more formative assessment(s) in each lesson that clearly connect to the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning goal(s). Candidate plans one summative assessment that clearly measures the FS\u2019s progress in meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate includes a rubric or performance criteria for the summative assessment that clearly measure the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goals for the unit plan. Candidate\u2019s planning accurately addresses foundational reading skill(s),\u2020 additional theme(s),\u2021 and integrated ELD.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate plans multiple formative assessments within each lesson of the unit to monitor the FS\u2019s ELA/Literacy and ELD understandings and learning needs.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus When developing the summative assessment and corresponding rubric or performance criteria, the candidate includes real-life scenarios that build upon the FS\u2019s culture, language(s), and/or experiences."], ["In their planning, the candidate does not leverage the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate does not plan to use UDL strategy(ies) when teaching the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD content. The unit plan does not include three lessons or the lessons do not align and/or build upon one another to create a progression of learning. Candidate does not plan to teach foundational reading skill(s)* and/or does not plan to teach foundational reading skill(s) using a direct, systematic, and explicit approach. Candidate does not include an additional theme** and/or does not plan to actively engage the FS while teaching the additional theme(s). Candidate\u2019s plan does not integrate ELD, and/or the ELD does not support the foundational reading skill(s)* and/or the additional theme(s).** Candidate does not include adaptation(s) that address the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests and/or learning needs. Candidate does not include a plan for collaboration with and/or facilitation of instructional support personnel.", "In their planning, the candidate vaguely leverages the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests. Candidate vaguely plans to use UDL strategy(ies) when teaching the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD content. The unit plan includes three lessons that vaguely align and/or build upon one another to create a progression of learning. When planning to teach the foundational reading skill(s),* candidate vaguely includes a direct, systematic, and explicit approach. Candidate vaguely plans to engage the FS with the additional theme(s).** Candidate\u2019s plan integrates ELD that vaguely supports the foundational reading skill(s)* and/or the additional theme(s).** Candidate includes adaptation(s) that vaguely address the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests and/or learning needs. Candidate includes a vague plan for collaboration with and/or facilitation of instructional support personnel.", "In their planning, the candidate clearly leverages student assets and/or interests. Candidate clearly plans to use appropriate UDL strategy(ies) when teaching the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD content. The unit plan includes three lessons that clearly align and build upon one another to create a progression of learning. When planning to teach the foundational reading skill(s),* candidate clearly includes a direct, systematic, and explicit approach. Candidate clearly plans to actively engage the FS with the additional theme(s).** Candidate\u2019s plan integrates ELD that clearly supports the foundational reading skill(s)* and the additional theme(s).** Candidate includes adaptation(s) that clearly address the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests and learning needs. Candidate includes a clear plan for collaboration with and/or facilitation of instructional support personnel.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate leverages the FS\u2019s assets by intentionally incorporating their cultural background, lived experiences, interests, and/or primary language into the lesson design.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Each of the candidate\u2019s lessons include multiple UDL strategies to support the FS toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD learning goal(s) based on their assets and/or interests and learning needs."], ["Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of how they teach the foundational reading skill(s)* using a direct and explicit approach. Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of how they actively engage the FS during the teaching of the foundational reading skill(s). Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of the literacy lesson(s) described in Step 1.", "Candidate includes an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they teach the foundational reading skill(s)* using a direct and explicit approach. Candidate includes an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they actively engage the FS during the teaching of the foundational reading skill(s). Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of the literacy lesson(s) described in Step 1.", "Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of how they teach the foundational reading skill(s)* using a direct and explicit approach. Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of how they actively engage the FS during the teaching of the foundational reading skill(s). Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of the literacy lesson(s) described in Step 1.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate models the targeted foundational reading skill(s) using precise academic language and think-alouds to make cognitive processes visible.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate formatively assesses the FS\u2019s foundational reading skill(s) throughout the lesson(s) and structures frequent opportunities for the FS to respond and receive feedback."], ["Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they leverage the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests while teaching the additional theme(s)* from the ELA/ELD framework. Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of how they actively engage the FS in learning the additional theme(s) from the ELA/ELD Framework.", "Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they leverage the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests while teaching the additional theme(s)* from the ELA/ELD framework. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they actively engage the FS in learning the additional theme(s) from the ELA/ELD Framework.", "Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they leverage the FS\u2019s assets and/or interests while teaching the additional theme(s)* from the ELA/ELD framework. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they actively engage the FS in learning the additional theme(s) from the ELA/ELD Framework.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate incorporates the FS\u2019s cultural background, lived experiences, interests, and/or primary language into instruction of the additional theme(s) from the ELA/ELD framework.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate provides structured opportunities for the FS to collaboratively explore the additional theme(s) through discussion, writing, and/or reading."], ["Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of UDL strategy(ies). Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they integrate ELD to support the teaching of the foundational reading skill(s) and/or the additional theme(s).", "Candidate includes an unclear demonstration and/or description of the UDL strategy(ies) they use to teach the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD content. Candidate provides an unclear demonstration and/or description of how they integrate ELD to support the teaching of the foundational reading skill(s) and/or the additional theme(s).", "Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of the UDL strategy(ies) they use to teach the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD content. Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they integrate ELD to support the teaching of the foundational reading skill(s) and/or the additional theme(s).", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate allows the FS to demonstrate mastery of foundational reading skills and/or the additional theme(s) orally, in writing, visually, or through performance.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of multiple UDL strategies used to support the teaching of the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning goals."], ["Candidate does not provide a demonstration and/or description of how they use formative assessment(s) to monitor the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals. Candidate does not include a demonstration and/or description of how they respond intentionally to formative assessment results to support the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals.", "Candidate provides a vague demonstration and/or description of how they use formative assessment(s) to monitor the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals. Candidate includes a vague demonstration and/or description of how they respond intentionally to formative assessment results to support the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals.", "Candidate provides a clear demonstration and description of how they use formative assessment(s) to monitor the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals. Candidate includes a clear demonstration and description of how they respond intentionally to formative assessment results to support the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD goals.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate uses multiple formative assessments, such as purposeful questioning, academic discussion, analysis of student work, and/or real-time checks for understanding, to monitor the FS\u2019s learning in relation to both ELA/Literacy and ELD goals.", "All of Levels 3 and 4, plus: Candidate analyzes student responses during instruction to identify patterns and any misconceptions. Based on this evidence, the candidate immediately adapts instruction in meaningful ways, including differentiating tasks, providing targeted scaffolds, and/or extending learning for the FS."], ["Candidate\u2019s reflection does not include an analysis of the FS\u2019s summative assessment results. Candidate does not identify understandings and/or misconceptions related to the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD goals, OR the candidate does not base their analysis on the information they gathered while teaching and/or the summative assessment results. Candidate does not provide specific, actionable feedback for the FS, OR the specific, actionable feedback is not based on the summative assessment results. Candidate does not provide a description of the impact of their instructional approach(es) or their choice of student activity(ies) during the unit for the FS. Candidate does not provide an explanation of what instructional changes they would make for the FS if they taught the unit again. Candidate does not provide feedback to the family/guardian(s) of the FS to support caregivers in understanding the assessment results and/or how they can support the FS\u2019s learning beyond the classroom.", "Candidate\u2019s reflection includes a vague analysis of the FS\u2019s summative assessment results. Based on their analysis of the summative assessment results and the information gathered during their teaching, the candidate vaguely identifies understandings and/or misconceptions related to the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD goals. Candidate provides feedback to the FS that is vague, not actionable, or not clearly based on the FS\u2019s performance on the summative assessment, OR the candidate provides developmentally inappropriate feedback. Candidate provides a vague description of the impact of their instructional approach(es) and/or their choice of student activity(ies) during the unit for the FS. Candidate provides a vague explanation of what instructional changes they would make for the FS if they taught the unit again. Candidate provides vague feedback to the family/guardian(s) of the FS to support caregivers in understanding the assessment results and/or how they can support the FS\u2019s learning beyond the classroom.", "Candidate\u2019s reflection includes a clear analysis of the FS\u2019s summative assessment results. Based on their analysis of the summative assessment results and the information gathered during their teaching, the candidate clearly identifies understandings and/or misconceptions related to the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and ELD goals. Candidate provides specific, actionable feedback for the FS that is clearly based on the FS\u2019s performance on the summative assessment. Candidate provides a clear description of the impact of their instructional approach(es) and their choice of student activity(ies) during the unit for the FS. Candidate provides a clear explanation of what instructional changes they would make for the FS if they taught the unit again. Candidate provides clear feedback to the family/guardian(s) of the FS to support caregivers in understanding the assessment results and how they can support the FS\u2019s learning beyond the classroom.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate\u2019s specific, actionable feedback for the FS is aligned to the learning goals of the unit. It clearly names what the FS did well and/or what needs improvement based on specific strengths and/or needs of the FS using concrete examples from the summative assessment and/or observations.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: When reflecting on the impact of their instruction, the candidate uses data from the unit plan, specific examples from their teaching or commentary, and data from formative and/or summative assessment(s) to determine which strategies moved learning forward."], ["Candidate does not include a plan for follow-up instruction for the FS, either re-teaching or extension, based on their analysis of the FS\u2019s performance during the unit, including summative assessment results. The video and commentary do not include either: \u2022 Re-Teach: A demonstration and/or description of the targeted intervention and/or individualized strategy used to support the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning goal(s) OR \u2022 Extend: A demonstration and/or description of the instruction that deepens and/or advances the FS\u2019s ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning Candidate does not include specific example(s) from Steps 1, 2, and/or 3 to support their follow-up instructional decision making, OR evidence cited does not support follow-up instructional decisions.", "Candidate includes a vague plan for follow-up instruction for the FS, either re-teaching or extension, based on their analysis of the FS\u2019s performance during the unit, including summative assessment results. The video and/or commentary include either: \u2022 Re-Teach: An unclear demonstration and/or description of the targeted intervention and/or individualized strategy used to support the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning goal(s) OR \u2022 Extend: An unclear demonstration and/or description of the instruction that deepens and/or advances the FS\u2019s ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning Candidate uses vague example(s) from Steps 1, 2, and/or 3 to support their follow-up instructional decision making.", "Candidate includes a clear plan for follow-up instruction for the FS, either re-teaching or extension, based on their analysis of the FS\u2019s performance during the unit, including summative assessment results. The video and commentary include either: \u2022 Re-Teach: A clear demonstration and description of the targeted intervention and/or individualized strategy used to support the FS\u2019s progress toward meeting the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning goal(s) OR \u2022 Extend: A clear demonstration and description of the instruction that deepens and/or advances the FS\u2019s ELA/Literacy and/or ELD learning Candidate clearly uses specific example(s) from Steps 1, 2, and/or 3 to support their follow-up instructional decision making.", "All of Level 3, plus: Candidate leverages the FS\u2019s assets by intentionally incorporating the FS\u2019s cultural, linguistic, and/or lived experiences into the follow-up instruction design.", "All of Levels 3 & 4, plus: Candidate synthesizes multiple sources of evidence from Steps 1, 2, and 3 to justify their instructional decisions and clearly explains how the selected strategy accelerates the FS\u2019s learning of the ELA/Literacy and/or ELD content."]]};
